// File completeness, competent service, silence rules and the monthly
// and expense duties (R. 544-1/2/3, D. 544-8 duty, D. 544-9/10).
//
// R. 544-1 builds the complete-file heads (claim, re-examination,
// renewal from 2024) from the employer attestation and the sealed
// medical certificate. R. 544-2 attributes competence to the child's
// health-cost service. R. 544-3 builds the elapsed silence months from
// the recorded months and deems the agreement (second month) and the
// decision (third month) favourable; the 2022-2024 renewal derogation
// deems them unfavourable instead and adds the notification duty; from
// 2024 the renewal silence is favourable like the initial request. The
// deemed agreement opens the right through the same channel as the
// recorded one. D. 544-8 makes the L. 5421-1 job-seeker declare the days
// taken to France Travail; D. 544-9 the five monthly supporting-document
// duties; D. 544-10 the monthly sworn expense declaration and the
// production of proof on demand. Each D. 544-9/10 duty instance and its
// performance carry the concerned month (mois_concerne_ajpp, first of
// the month); «chaque mois au plus» is read as the monthly proof rhythm
// (package map, D3-D9): one transmission per concerned month satisfies
// that month, with no over-frequency prohibition modelled.

language "law.core" version "0.2";
package fr.pf.ajpp version "0.1.0";
namespace "urn:fr:corpus:clir:pf-ajpp";

